  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation for Indonesia&apos;s School Children (INOVASI) Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The INOVASI Phase 3 program builds on the work, and lessons learned, from previous phases which focused on improving students&#x2019; foundational skills, particularly literacy, numeracy, and character education. INOVASI is an adaptive program which trials, learns from and improves collective and localised system approaches in implementing relevant education policies and reforms by working in five educational levers. These include curriculum and assessment, teaching practices, school leadership, GEDSI, and climate resilience. INOVASI continues to work in East Java, North Kalimantan, West Nusa Tenggara, and East Nusa Tenggara provinces. In this phase, INOVASI has expanded to additional provinces&#x2014;Maluku, West Java, and the Capital City of Nusantara&#x2014;making it six provinces in total. INOVASI has also widened the scope from early grades to one-year pre-primary until sixth grade of primary school.</narrative>
  </description>
